cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GRsuite: the airGR suite of GR rainfall-runoff models, in Python"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata — and cite
  airGR, which GRsuite reimplements, together with the reference of the model
  you actually ran (see docs/REFERENCES.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bouhafa
    given-names: Najim
    email: najimbouhafa@gmail.com
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Najim33/GRsuite"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of the GR suite of lumped rainfall-runoff models
  (GR1A, GR2M, GR4J, GR5J, GR6J, GR4H, GR5H) and of the CemaNeige snow module,
  translated from the R package airGR 1.7.9 and validated against it.
  GRsuite originates no new hydrology: every model, criterion and algorithm is
  the work of the authors cited below.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - rainfall-runoff
  - GR4J
  - CemaNeige
  - airGR
  - streamflow
  - calibration
references:
